<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="031" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Analysis tools: spaarke_start_analysis, spaarke_get_analysis</title>
    <phase>2 Long-running work, AI, widgets, task writes</phase>
    <gate>BLOCKED until spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1 PR #3161 and r1 task 042 have merged to master and master is merged into this branch (merge, never rebase)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Model-callable write that must reuse AnalysisAuthorizationFilter's create check through a shared method (an extraction no Phase 0 task covers); tags include auth</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Includes an authorization extraction from AnalysisAuthorizationFilter with frozen REST bytes (same class of work as 007); raised from the default because the spec's plan had no prerequisite task for it</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>H</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Analysis/**, AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.cs and the Analysis ledger partial; no other Phase 2 task touches them</parallel-reason>
    <deps>020</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, ai, auth, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>5-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add spaarke_start_analysis (model-callable, reversible, idempotency key) that creates an sprk_analysis through the same RecordCreationService.CreateAsync path POST /api/ai/analysis/create uses, after the same create authorization (moved from AnalysisAuthorizationFilter into a shared method, REST bytes frozen), and returns a deep link into the Analysis Workspace without running the analysis; and spaarke_get_analysis (read-only) over GET /api/ai/analysis/{analysisId}.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in the Spaarke Dataverse write path (RecordCreationService) and MCP tool handlers.</role>
  <goal>A tool-created analysis equals a REST-created one for the same inputs; refusals match REST reasonCodes through one shared authorization method; a retried start creates one record; get returns the REST analysis (slimmed) or a uniform not-found.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-06, NFR-06. REST: Api/Ai/AnalysisEndpoints.cs (group /api/ai/analysis; POST /create :70 with AddAnalysisCreateAuthorizationFilter — checks, as the caller, Create on sprk_analysis and analysis.attach (Read + AppendTo) on the source; handler calls RecordCreationService.CreateAsync at ~:195; GET /{analysisId} :137). Filter: Api/Filters/AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.cs. Write-path rules: docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md. Pattern for the shared method: task 007 (PlaybookAuthorizationFilter) and 008 (FinanceAuthorizationFilter).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.cs (create check exposed as a public method; the filter calls it)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Analysis/StartAnalysisTool.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Analysis/GetAnalysisTool.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Mcp.Analysis.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Ai/AnalysisCreateContractBaselineTests.cs (frozen REST bytes, recorded before the extraction)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/Analysis/AnalysisToolsContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Mcp/Analysis/AnalysisToolsAuthTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/AnalysisEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/Signals/SignalRoutesContractBaselineTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">General McpToolResults, ledger partials</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">BLOCKED until r1 PR #3161 and r1 task 042 are merged to master and master is merged into this branch (merge, never rebase).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Run as the caller (IHttpContextAccessor; UserContextRequired; no app-only fallback; never pass or log the token). The create check moves into one public method the filter and the tool both call; the tool adds no check of its own (spec MUST NOT copy authorization).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">The frozen-bytes baseline for POST /api/ai/analysis/create (201, 400, 403, 404) is written and green before the extraction and passes unchanged after it; the filter stays registered the same way.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">The record is created only through RecordCreationService.CreateAsync (one server-side owner); no direct Dataverse create; the tool never executes the analysis (no AnalysisOrchestrationService call).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">spaarke_start_analysis: readOnlyHint false, destructiveHint false, idempotentHint true; required idempotencyKey; a retry with the same key and caller returns the first analysis id. spaarke_get_analysis: readOnlyHint true. Deep link built with the existing Analysis Workspace link helper (find it; do not hand-build). Ledger rows in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Mcp.Analysis.cs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Model-visible: analysis id, name, status, source document name, link; no analysis output text beyond a ≤ 500-char summary. Logs: tool name, latency, outcome, correlation id.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source: spec.md 'Placement &amp; New Components'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, 55 MB total triggers architecture review, 60 MB is a hard stop. No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Before each push run bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master. CS0618 is a build error: migrate, never suppress.</constraint>
  </constraints>

