  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Confirm the r1 gate and 020; read CreateAnalysis, GetAnalysis and AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.</step>
    <step order="2">Write AnalysisCreateContractBaselineTests and confirm it passes on the unchanged code.</step>
    <step order="3">Expose the create check as a public method; the filter calls it; the baseline still passes.</step>
    <step order="4">Write the two tools and ledger rows; write contract and auth tests; run MCP suites, analysis tests, ArchTests and conformance.</step>
    <step order="5">Measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="7">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the create check cannot be exposed without changing REST bytes, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
    <trigger>If idempotency needs a new store, STOP and escalate with the §11 answers.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>POST /api/ai/analysis/create (AnalysisEndpoints.cs) over RecordCreationService.CreateAsync with AnalysisAuthorizationFilter; GET /api/ai/analysis/{id}; notes/reuse-scan.md row "Analysis create".</existing>
    <extension>The filter is extended in place (its check becomes a public method, as 007/008 do); the tools are thin adapters.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Copilot users cannot start an analysis on a document (FR-06 fails); without the shared method the tool would have to copy the check, which the spec forbids.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build; dotnet test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Analysis/StartAnalysisTool.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Analysis/GetAnalysisTool.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Ai/AnalysisCreateContractBaselineTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/Analysis/AnalysisToolsContractTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/Mcp/Analysis/AnalysisToolsAuthTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">AnalysisCreateContractBaselineTests pass before and after the extraction (201/400/403/404 bytes identical).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The tool-created record's fields equal a REST-created one for the same inputs (captured at RecordCreationService's boundary); the returned link opens the Analysis Workspace for that id.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A retried start with the same key creates one record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: missing Create privilege or analysis.attach refusal returns isError with the REST reasonCode and creates nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the tool never calls AnalysisOrchestrationService (asserted).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ArchTests and conformance pass; publish-size delta recorded; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-06, NFR-06. Two adversarial-verifier passes (auth). uac-r2 and ontology-r1 review the extraction.</notes>

